The function was simplified to reduce branching and avoid a conditional jump by directly using the ternary operator, which compilers often optimize better than explicit if-statements for simple cases like this.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsMaxCadenceValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(18);
        return (field != FIT_NULL) ? field->IsValueValid() : FIT_FALSE;
    }
